{
 "about": "Upper panel ornament of the left door leaf of the Garden Gate (plate 4, 'North Side of Garden Gate'), left half, drawn by hand as smooth curves while viewing the University of Manchester copy of the 1786 engravings online (PR-CHCR-00457, image 26). Only these hand-drawn control points are used; no pixels of that scan. Coordinates are that scan's pixels. Curves are Catmull-Rom splines through the points; polylines are straight. The right half is the mirror image. Scroll, horn and the ribbon to the centre are one raised form; the bud is a band open to the left with the arrow inside it. The raised border runs out to the panel edge, so the ground is only the marked pockets.",
